    canberraContext: 'Deck surfaces in Canberra can face strong summer sun, winter moisture and temperature swings. Boards exposed at a deck edge may weather differently from those under a roof, and shaded areas can stay damp longer. Tell us where the damaged section sits relative to trees, sprinklers and runoff. This helps frame material and finish choices, as well as whether repeated wetting has affected the structure beneath the visible surface.',
    enquiry: 'Send wide photos from above and from the side, close views of damaged boards or fixings, and underside photos only where safely accessible. Estimate deck dimensions, height above ground and the number of affected boards. Say whether a hatch, open edge or crawl space allows underside access; do not enter a confined or unstable space to collect photos. Note any movement, handrail or stair concern, your Canberra suburb and access through the property. Describe the existing finish if known and whether water regularly sits on the surface. You can attach photos to the enquiry; further material can be shared later if requested.',
